ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Specify number of layers (= number of interfaces -1)
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
1          c: Number of layers in model
2          c: Number of velocity grid types (1 or 2)
0.02       c: Pinchout distance (km) (>=0.0)
vgrids.in  c: Output velocity grid file
interfaces.in c: Output interface grid file
145678     c: Seed for random number generation (int)

ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Set 3-D grid size and location.
c Radial range is relative to Earth's surface (km): top, bottom
c Lat: N-S (deg), Lon: E-W (deg, East-positive)
c grid3dg automatically adds cushion boundary nodes to the defined grid.
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
  0.0   -70.0    c: Radial range (top-bottom) of grid (km)
 20.0    35.0    c: Latitudinal range (N-S) of grid (degrees)
 96.0   109.0    c: Longitudinal range (E-W) of grid (degrees)
6371.0           c: Earth radius

ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Set up propagation grid file (propgrid.in) for fm3d
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
propgrid.in  c: Name of propagation grid file
21 41 41     c: Number of points in rad lat, long
5 5          c: Refine factor & no. of local cells
0.05         c: Cushion factor for prop grid (<<1)

ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Set velocity grid values for layer 1
c (two entries per line because velocity grid types = 2)
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
12 12        c: Number of radial grid points (type 1 & 2)
12 12        c: Number of grid points in theta (N-S) (type 1 & 2)
12 12        c: Number of grid points in phi (E-W) (type 1 & 2)
0            c: Use model (0) or constant gradient (1)
P            c: Use P or S velocity model
velo_fm3d.txt c: Velocity model (option 0)
3            c: Dimension of velocity model (1=1-D,3=3-D)
5.4 4.0      c: Velocity at origin (km/s) (option 1)  [dummy if option 0]
7.0 5.0      c: Velocity at maximum depth (km/s) (option 1) [dummy if option 0]

ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Optionally apply random structure to layer 1  (turn off)
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
0            c: Add random structure (0=no,1=yes)
1.0          c: Std of Gaussian noise (ignored if 0)
0            c: Add a priori model covariance (0=no,1=yes)?
0.3          c: Diagonal elements of covariance matrix (if used)

ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Optionally apply checkerboard to layer 1 (turn off)
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
0            c: Add checkerboard (0=no,1=yes)
1.0          c: Max perturbation (ignored if 0)
2            c: Checkerboard size (N×N×N)
0            c: Use spacing (0=no,1=yes)

ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Optionally apply spike to layer 1 (turn off)
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
0            c: Add spike (0=no,1=yes)
0.0          c: Spike amplitude
0.0 0.0 0.0  c: Spike location (r,theta,phi) or (z,lat,lon) depending on code notes

ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Defining the interface grids
c For M layers => M+1 interfaces. Here M=1 => 2 interfaces.
c Horizontal node distribution must be identical for all interfaces.
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
12           c: Number of grid points in theta (N-S)
12           c: Number of grid points in phi (E-W)

ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Set up interface grid for interface 1 (top)
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
0            c: Obtain grid from external file (0=no,1=yes)
interface1.z c: External interface grid file (option 1)
0.0          c: Height of NW grid point (option 0)
0.0          c: Height of NE grid point (option 0)
0.0          c: Height of SW grid point (option 0)

ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
c Set up interface grid for interface 2 (bottom)
ccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccccc
0
interface2.z
-70.0
-70.0
-70.0
